The install has **two sides**. Do them in order.

---

## Side A — Prep machine (HAS internet)

A machine with internet access that can also reach your private registry.

**Tooling:** bash ≥4.2, GNU coreutils, tar ≥1.34, wget, docker (runs the bundled
skopeo), cosign ≥2.4.1.

1. Copy `01-prepare.sh` to the prep machine.
2. Run it:
   ```bash
   ./01-prepare.sh
   ```
   It downloads and cosign-verifies the airgap bundle, pushes all images and
   charts to `{{.Registry}}`, and downloads + verifies the k0s binaries
   ({{range $i, $a := .Architectures}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}`{{$.K0sBinaryPrefix}}-{{$a}}`{{end}}).
3. Move the downloaded k0s binaries into the airgap (USB, internal transfer,
   etc.) alongside the `02-fileserver/` directory.

> **Do not rename the k0s binary.** Child cluster deployment depends on the
> exact filename `{{.PrimaryK0sBinary}}`.

---

## Side B — Airgapped management cluster

**Tooling:** kubectl + helm ≥3.16.3 against a management cluster (Kubernetes
≥1.30) with a `StorageClass` and a LoadBalancer provider.

### 1. Stand up the k0s fileserver
```bash
kubectl apply -f 02-fileserver/namespace-pvc.yaml
kubectl apply -f 02-fileserver/binary-loader.yaml
# copy the k0s binary into the PVC (expects the binary in the current dir):
./02-fileserver/load-k0s.sh
kubectl apply -f 02-fileserver/configmap-nginx.yaml
kubectl apply -f 02-fileserver/deployment-service.yaml
```

Get the external IP and confirm the binary is served:
```bash
kubectl get svc k0s-fileserver -n {{.FileserverNamespace}} --watch
EXTERNAL_IP="$(kubectl get svc k0s-fileserver -n {{.FileserverNamespace}} -o jsonpath='{.status.loadBalancer.ingress[0].ip}')"
curl -I "http://${EXTERNAL_IP}/{{.RegistryProject}}/{{.PrimaryK0sBinary}}"
```
Expect `HTTP/1.1 200 OK`. Make sure this URL matches `fileserverURL`
(`{{.FileserverURL}}`) in your config — update `03-values.yaml` if the
LoadBalancer IP differs from what you configured.

### 2. Install k0rdent Enterprise
```bash
./04-install.sh
```
This runs `helm install kcm {{.ChartsRepoURL}}/k0rdent-enterprise --version {{.KcmVersion}} -n {{.Namespace}} --create-namespace -f 03-values.yaml`.

### 3. Verify (wait 5–10 minutes first)
```bash
./05-verify.sh
```
Expect ~30 pods `Running` in `{{.Namespace}}`, ~10 in `projectsveltos`,
`Management` READY = `True`, and all templates VALID.

---

## Notes

- **Non-authenticated registry.** These artifacts assume the registry does not
  require authentication (the v1.4.0 default). If yours does, you will also need
  image-pull and registry-credential secrets plus extra `values.yaml` keys — not
  generated here.
{{- if .SelfSignedCA}}
- **Self-signed CA.** `04-install.sh` creates the `{{.CACertSecretName}}` secret
  from `./ca.crt` (override with `CA_CERT_PATH`) before installing. Ensure that
  CA signs both the registry and fileserver certificates.
{{- end}}
- **Offline cosign.** `01-prepare.sh` runs on the internet-connected prep
  machine, so signature verification uses the online transparency log. For fully
  offline verification, fetch `cosign.pub` separately and consult the Mirantis
  docs for the current offline flag.
- **Image coverage.** Cross-check pushed images against Mirantis's
  `full_images_list.txt` for your version:
  `{{.BundleBaseURL}}/{{.KcmVersion}}/full_images_list.txt`
